        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పట్టుబట్టు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పట్టుబట్టు — paṭṭubaṭṭu — \"to insist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆమె ఆ రోజే వెళ్ళాలని పట్టుబట్టింది. āme ā rōjē veḷḷālani paṭṭubaṭṭindi. She insisted on going that very day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): పట్టుబట్టాను, paṭṭubaṭṭānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పట్టు, a grip, + పట్టు, to hold: to keep a firm grip on one’s point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పట్టుబట్టు (paṭṭubaṭṭu) is native Dravidian, a compound of paṭṭu, \"a hold, a grasp; perseverance\", and paṭṭu, \"to hold, to seize\" (DEDR 4034)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
